COMP 324 - Project 
TripJoy — Travel Planning Website
TripJoy is a travel planning website developed for COMP 324 at Loyola University Chicago. It helps users explore cities around the world, discover popular attractions, and save places they are interested in visiting.

The goal of TripJoy is to make vacation planning easier by bringing destination discovery and favorite attractions together in one place.

Features
City Search: Search for a destination by city name using the Travel Advisor API.
Popular Destinations: Browse featured cities, including London, Paris, New York City, Tokyo, Dubai, Barcelona, Rome, and Madrid.
Attraction Discovery: Retrieve and browse attractions associated with a selected destination.
Favorites: Save interesting attractions to a favorites list and remove them when they are no longer needed.
Map Integration: View a map on the favorites page using Mapbox to support trip planning.
Persistent Browser Storage: Use browser localStorage to retain search results and saved favorites between page visits.

Technologies Used
HTML5 — Page structure and content
CSS3 — Styling, layouts, and visual presentation
JavaScript — Search functionality, API requests, favorites management, and browser storage
Travel Advisor API (RapidAPI) — Destination search and attraction data
Mapbox GL JS — Interactive map integration
Google Fonts — Montserrat typography
